    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.21), whose matchup against Kumar Rocker is the cornerstone of our offensive strategy. With a favorable platoon edge and a projected leadoff spot, **Gunnar Henderson** holds our highest efficiency score, capitalizing on a SP skill profile that plays perfectly into his strengths. Following closely, **Kyle Tucker** (75.28) and **Andy Pages** (74.43) are poised for high-impact performances against Eduardo Rodriguez. Both benefit significantly from Rodriguez\u2019s high xERA and favorable park factors; notably, **Andy Pages** receives a marginal boost from the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which may provide the extra half-step needed to generate stolen base opportunities\u2014a critical priority given our organizational focus on elite speed.\n\nThe depth of our roster necessitated a difficult choice at the utility spot, where **Nasim Nunez** (58.06) narrowly edged out **Coby Mayo** (45.68). While **Coby Mayo** offers clear power potential, his projected spot in the bottom third of the order, combined with a negative platoon variance against Rocker, dropped him well below our efficiency threshold. Conversely, **Nasim Nunez** maintains a higher floor due to his versatility and the favorable matchup against Singer, despite a slight drag from his batting position. We remain vigilant regarding the 39% rain risk hanging over **Miguel Vargas**; while he is currently slated to start, should the weather turn, we are prepared to pivot to more stable options. We have elected to keep **Luis Robert Jr.** on the bench today, as he faces a challenging matchup against Jones; the combination of a tough opponent and a negative platoon split makes him a candidate to preserve game caps rather than force a low-efficiency start.",
